sses the case with which Sugrīva travelled the earth; like a fire brand whirled conveys his vehement speed; and like the image reflected on a mirror signifies the lucidity of his perception.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.786,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-46-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4045011","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"cddda9aaa5ef5704c30ec7ab534c6983897cc710e0a6ebc378fc4efeea3650a3","compact":"f2420f54c10369c316b3c8e66f536868a00845d5926b4a4bacdbb801720cd4aa","nasal":"fae0fcc82f91cf2de20d5e6d50d4c40fe592d55c164dd2860b56085f12387762"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-45-12","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":45,"verse":12,"english":"Hotly pursued and chased by Vāli, I surveyed various streams and woods and cities. And I surveyed the earth like the hoof-print of a cow, or the image reflected from a mirror, or a firebrand whirled (in the air).* *The commentator remarks that like the hoof-print of a cow expresses the case with which Sugrīva travelled the earth; like a fire brand whirled conveys his vehement speed; and like the image reflected on a mirror signifies the lucidity of his perception.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.811,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-46-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4045012","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"26224474450666a48e563fc17d529281cd782053d6be789d225ee4968b7f9829","compact":"e657326e52688b2036f0a0815b486afeb3a72597d6336d5451e04417670e4f25","nasal":"e657326e52688b2036f0a0815b486afeb3a72597d6336d5451e04417670e4f25"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-45-13","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":45,"verse":13,"english":"And that heroic monkey Satavali swiftly set out for the northern regions covered by the monarch of mountains.","alignment":{"type":"approximate","confidence":0.505,"method":"fuzzy-nearby-witness","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-45-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4045013","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d5060ccb44ba17944960077833eb37b284eb5db888c72701c0cf45a0d5f1dc1c","compact":"f6b342b54c42e08f972c6a79a2db001b0c8539a45c2bab670e4f82b245262389","nasal":"b91a5235a3b92310de9b01ee0825ebd164bb61ee153fa03b35a3185135321019"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-45-14","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":45,"verse":14,"english":"'O king, now, I remember me how that lord of monkeys, Vāli, was cursed by Matanga in this very hermitage. If Vāli enters (into this asylum), his head becomes cleft in hundred.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-46-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4045014","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c175de681185628b01e38a5038063b5713b6a1616d29dd10156a7d85defddad7","compact":"0e1f34016af78e604028648f7e6cc294cf096ee430a7d73f6feb93eb6bb10b26","nasal":"b279661db15f93d2949d574655667ba0b86e831ec92c47eadfefed69547c358e"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-45-15","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":45,"verse":15,"english":"'O king, now, I remember me how that lord of monkeys, Vāli, was cursed by Matanga in this very hermitage. If Vāli enters (into this asylum), his head becomes cleft in hundred. There shall dwell happily without anxiety.' O king's son, thereupon, we went to the Rișyamuka mountain, nor did then Vāli enter we there from fear of Matanga.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.463,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-46-17","DUTT-4-46-18"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4045015","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"947a9c918dee17e6d14bbe3c1077ff3fb1d4406645e39534a74b2be693cd9134","compact":"12ea700c592f0014f7fc3f6e267fcccab42552a44